 Requirements:
 -------------
 This install requires WHDLoad 17 or newer and DIC to be in the path.
 These programs can be found in the WHDLoad package.
 To install from a different drive than DF0: select installation mode Expert.

 The installed game requires 0.5 MB ChipMem and 0.5 MB OtherMem
 (+0.9 MB for preload).
 It can be quit by pressing Del (key can be changed with Tooltype "QuitKey=").


 Features:
 --------
 - Full load from HD
 - Protection removed (manual check)
 - Interrupts fixed
 - Manual and hints included
 - Lots of icons by various authors included
 - Source code included (also on GitHub: https://github.com/Vesuri/whdload)
 - Quit option that works on 68000 machines


  

 High frame rate support:
 ------------------------
 Version 4.0b is a beta contribution by Vesuri, based on StingRay's v3.0.

 The installer sets CUSTOM1=1 in the game icon, so the option is on in a
 new installation; CUSTOM1=0 (or unselecting "High frame rate support" in
 the WHDLoad splash window) restores the original game. It requires a 68020
 or better with the game in Fast RAM. Other machines run the original game.

 Use the WHDLoad tooltype DCACHE (or at least CACHE) for the best speed.
 The slave leaves cache settings to WHDLoad. Example from the Shell:

 WHDLoad Indianapolis500.Slave PRELOAD CUSTOM1=1 CACHE DCACHE

 The option removes the original frame-rate limit, smooths motion between
 simulation ticks, and uses CPU drawing where it is faster than the blitter.
 Game logic and simulation speed are unchanged. While driving, the camera
 and player's car are predicted, so wall hits, hard braking or steering
 reversals can overshoot briefly. Opponents advance by their native rates.
 The demo and instant replays use interpolation.

 Only the slave, its source, this ReadMe and the installer (which writes
 CUSTOM1=1) differ from StingRay's v3.0 install package. To update an
 existing installation, copy Indianapolis500.slave into the installed
 drawer and add CUSTOM1=1 (and DCACHE) to the game icon.

 The beta has been checked in FS-UAE; real-hardware testing is outstanding.


 History:
 --------
 version 4.0b (11/11/2026), high frame rate support by Vesuri:
 - high frame rate support (CUSTOM1=1), enabled in the installed icon
 - 68020+ and Fast RAM required; original behavior on other machines
 - smooth driving motion and CPU drawing optimizations
 - smooth instant replay motion with the original transition-wipe pace
 - audio DMA wait fixed: the music no longer loses notes on fast CPUs
   (68040/060)

 version 3.0 (30/04/2022) done by StingRay:
 - patch redone
 - saves are done to separated files now (issue #5601)
 - manual protection completely skipped
 - interrupts fixed
 - default quitkey changed to Del
 - new install script

 version 2.1 (26/11/2020) done by JOTD:
 - quit key with 68000 (issue #0004864)
 - source code rework
 
 version 2.0 (24/11/2002) done by JOTD:
 - Uses 68060 caches & fast memory for better framerate
 - Rewritten installer script
 - Adapted to Barfly/WHDLoad 13+
 - added a great choice of icons by various authors
 - Reworked readme file
 - Manual included
 - Source included

 version 1.1 (05/08/1998) done by Dark Angel:
 - Instant replay now enabled but 1 MB chip required
 - Caches now by default on

 version 1.0 done by Dark Angel:
 - Initial release
 - Protection removed
 - Saves to HD
 - Return to OS (Numl)
 

